{"4262150": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Black Mountain of Tlaltecuhtli", "steam_appid": 4262150, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "dlc": [4844030], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Reality shifts. Rooms reset. The mountain remembers.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Black Mountain of Tlaltecuhtli is a third-person supernatural action-adventure set inside a living Aztec mountain that rewrites reality around you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a bounty hunter who tracked a target to the mountain and discovered a research bunker hidden in its core. What you found tore holes in reality. Now you can shift between dimensions at will. Fight hostile survivors and reality-warping entities, scavenge experimental weapons, and survive a mountain that watches, remembers, and punishes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.mp4?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Dimension Shifting &amp; Loop Zones</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Scientists studying the mountain discovered pockets of time they called Loop Zones. Areas that reset, reconfigure, and overlap. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Paths you crossed an hour ago are suddenly different. Hallways rearrange themselves. Symbols you could swear were not there before begin to match the ones in your nightmares. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Switch dimensions during combat and exploration. Modern bunker corridors become ancient Aztec temple halls. Debris blocking your path? Shift to a reality where it never fell. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The mountain feels less like a place and more like something with a memory. Reality feels edited, and you're learning to edit back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/fdfee7dfb826be4f7bb9bd86e29824ef.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/fdfee7dfb826be4f7bb9bd86e29824ef.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Combat &amp; Exploration </strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fight hostile survivors and reality-warped entities using cover-based gunplay, stealth, and vertical climbing.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Experimental weapons and prototype tech are scattered across both realities. Scavenge what you can.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Loop Zones can reset mid-fight, forcing you to adapt as the environment changes around you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you go, the worse it gets.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What Lies Beneath</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This bunker was not built here by accident. Long before the facility, the Aztecs carved chambers into this mountain to imprison something they feared enough to seal away forever.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Modern experiments weakened that prison. You made it worse. Now what the Aztecs feared is breaking free.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/4cddfc3a4249944ccd878348e1f3fb55.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/4cddfc3a4249944ccd878348e1f3fb55.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dimension-Switching Mechanics</strong> - Jump between realities during combat, exploration, and puzzle-solving Loop Zones  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Loop Zones</strong> - Environments reset and reconfigure over time, revealing new paths </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Third-Person Action</strong> - Cover-based combat, stealth, and vertical climbing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Experimental Arsenal</strong> - Advanced weapons and tech from both dimensions </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Aztec Mythology</strong> - Ancient temples, carved chambers, and ritual sites reveal the civilization that sealed the entity away</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every victory feels like pushing deeper into a story you weren't meant to find.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Reality shifts. Rooms reset. The mountain remembers.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Black Mountain of Tlaltecuhtli is a third-person supernatural action-adventure set inside a living Aztec mountain that rewrites reality around you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a bounty hunter who tracked a target to the mountain and discovered a research bunker hidden in its core. What you found tore holes in reality. Now you can shift between dimensions at will. Fight hostile survivors and reality-warping entities, scavenge experimental weapons, and survive a mountain that watches, remembers, and punishes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/3c90d3cae19f4a0eac9c3c2351388ea9.mp4?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Dimension Shifting &amp; Loop Zones</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Scientists studying the mountain discovered pockets of time they called Loop Zones. Areas that reset, reconfigure, and overlap. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Paths you crossed an hour ago are suddenly different. Hallways rearrange themselves. Symbols you could swear were not there before begin to match the ones in your nightmares. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Switch dimensions during combat and exploration. Modern bunker corridors become ancient Aztec temple halls. Debris blocking your path? Shift to a reality where it never fell. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The mountain feels less like a place and more like something with a memory. Reality feels edited, and you're learning to edit back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/fdfee7dfb826be4f7bb9bd86e29824ef.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/fdfee7dfb826be4f7bb9bd86e29824ef.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Combat &amp; Exploration </strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fight hostile survivors and reality-warped entities using cover-based gunplay, stealth, and vertical climbing.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Experimental weapons and prototype tech are scattered across both realities. Scavenge what you can.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Loop Zones can reset mid-fight, forcing you to adapt as the environment changes around you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you go, the worse it gets.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What Lies Beneath</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This bunker was not built here by accident. Long before the facility, the Aztecs carved chambers into this mountain to imprison something they feared enough to seal away forever.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Modern experiments weakened that prison. You made it worse. Now what the Aztecs feared is breaking free.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/4cddfc3a4249944ccd878348e1f3fb55.poster.avif?t=1787256177\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/extras/4cddfc3a4249944ccd878348e1f3fb55.webm?t=1787256177\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dimension-Switching Mechanics</strong> - Jump between realities during combat, exploration, and puzzle-solving Loop Zones  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Loop Zones</strong> - Environments reset and reconfigure over time, revealing new paths </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Third-Person Action</strong> - Cover-based combat, stealth, and vertical climbing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Experimental Arsenal</strong> - Advanced weapons and tech from both dimensions </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Aztec Mythology</strong> - Ancient temples, carved chambers, and ritual sites reveal the civilization that sealed the entity away</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every victory feels like pushing deeper into a story you weren't meant to find.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Third-person supernatural action-adventure in a living Aztec mountain. Climb collapsing ruins, shift dimensions to fight reality-warped enemies, and navigate Loop Zones where environments reset. The deeper you go, the closer you come to what the Aztecs sealed away.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/4e386b7556670bde4036dbddaebe5b82d0259c39/header.jpg?t=1787256177", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/e2885383aeb811a06bc27b3d7c3ce7ca80b7f836/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1787256177", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4262150/e2885383aeb811a06bc27b3d7c3ce7ca80b7f836/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1787256177", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 11<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> AMD: Ryzen 5 5600X or Ryzen 5 7600/Intel i7: Core i7-10700K or i7-12700K<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GTX 1060 / RX 580, 8–16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 20 GB available space</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Require